68
00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:23.950
I think he's missing fun.

69
00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.100
I would say you need a little fun in there too.

70
00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.990
Can we add a fifth one?
(audience applauds)

71
00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:30.410
Gotta have fun.

72
00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:31.840
He says, they're all important though

73
00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:33.650
and asked students to assess which areas

74
00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:34.870
they might be neglecting,

75
00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:36.760
because that's where they need to do their work.

76
00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:37.790
And if you think about it,

77
00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.470
those are the areas in your life where, you know,

78
00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:43.150
you can have three of those four going right,

79
00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:44.470
but that one little thing, you know,

80
00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:45.400
if work's not going right,

81
00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.980
it's hard to focus on the rest, you know?

82
00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:52.860
I love that this class has been created and developed

83
00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:57.660
and within seconds of the doors opening

84
00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.808
and the seats being able to be filled,

85
00:02:59.808 --> 00:03:01.210
(snaps fingers) attendance goes like that.

86
00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:02.290
You can't get in.
Mm.

87
00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:06.960
And I feel like this approach to the spiritual,

88
00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.833 line:15%
the mental wellness, the happiness,

89
00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:13.743 line:15%
our work life balance.

90
00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:18.270 line:15%
It's so funny that we go to these institutions

91
00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:21.800
and we're not focusing as much on the life

92
00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.950
as we are the learning.
Mm.

93
00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:25.440
And um,

94
00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:26.660
(audience applauds)
Interesting

95
00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:30.960
I think what's great is to,

96
00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.970
