99
00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:41.620
for them being more available.

100
00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:44.890
And the thing about college, unlike regular school,

101
00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:46.600
which makes me have an "aha" moment

102
00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.750
about why the debate is so rich,

103
00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:51.570
is because so much of college is elective.

104
00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:53.880
Oh.
Versus lower schools.

105
00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.230
So I'm glad to see this available.

106
00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:57.260
Well, I am too.

107
00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:58.590
I think it says something that

108
00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.750
these happiness classes filled up so fast.

109
00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.690
I mean, that's, there's a demand for it.

110
00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:05.581
And as somebody who was forced to take calculus,

111
00:04:05.581 --> 00:04:06.670
(chuckles) okay.
(audience laughs)

112
00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:09.550
I could have used a happiness class at some point.

113
00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:10.383
It would've been nice.

114
00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:13.640
But I think that maybe them showing that the demand is there

115
00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.460
will make other schools offer something like this as well.

116
00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:20.820
And I think the word happiness gets a really bad rap

117
00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:25.820
as if it is some lofty, hippy-dippy, silly notion.

118
00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:26.923
Right?

119
00:04:26.923 --> 00:04:30.260
And it is a war you will fight every day

120
00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:32.650
